  "id": "reward-expectancy",
  "term": "reward expectancy",
  "definition": "Reward expectancy is the anticipated likelihood or value of getting a reward in response to a particular cue or action. In the source, it is reflected in how strongly behavior is directed toward stimuli that predict reward, compared with similar stimuli that predict less or no reward.",
